From: WebKit upstream (Nic; reviewed by Carlos Garcia Campos)
Subject: [GTK][Skia] ShareableBitmap::paint ignores CompositeOperator::Copy
Upstream: https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/commit/645ce1764ad44d709b8ddfdcfd564fd06d1d8dc6
Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319864

Backport to the pinned 2.50.4 source. Transparent backing-store updates must
replace old pixels rather than accumulate thumbnail trails and scrim opacity.
All non-Copy callers retain the default SrcOver behavior. No sandbox changes.

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/skia/ShareableBitmapSkia.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/skia/ShareableBitmapSkia.cpp
@@ -87 +87,4 @@
-    context.platformContext()->drawImageRect(image.get(), scaledSrcRect, scaledDestRect, { }, nullptr, { });
+    SkPaint paint;
+    if (context.compositeMode().operation == CompositeOperator::Copy)
+        paint.setBlendMode(SkBlendMode::kSrc);
+    context.platformContext()->drawImageRect(image.get(), scaledSrcRect, scaledDestRect, { }, &paint, { });
